;;;;
;;;; Quality Requirements for the SBOM Tool (arc42 section 10)
;;;;
;;;; Derived from README, AGENTS.md and dev/plans. Measures are only given where the
;;;; sources state a verifiable criterion; no numeric targets are defined.
#{{:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/offline-by-default
   :name "offline by default"
   :desc "The tool makes no network calls unless a live vulnerability source is explicitly selected."
   :doc "### Scenario

A user or CI job runs the tool on SBOM files without -D/--vulnerability-source. Reports contain only what the SBOM and VEX files provide.

### Measure

No network access happens with the default option :none (verifiable by running without network access). Source: README (\"fully offline\"), dev/plans/deps-dev-vulnerability-adapter.md.

### Quality attribute

Security and privacy (no component data leaves the machine unasked), reliability in restricted CI networks."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/offline-deterministic-tests
   :name "offline, fast and deterministic test suite"
   :desc "bb test needs no network access and gives the same result on every run."
   :doc "### Scenario

A developer or CI job runs bb test.

### Measure

All tests pass without network access. The vulnerability adapters' real HTTP calls are deliberately not tested; only their pure mapping and chunking logic is (see risk network-paths-untested). Source: the Verification sections of dev/plans/*.md. No duration target is defined.

### Quality attribute

Testability."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/jvm-and-babashka-portability
   :name "runs on the JVM and under babashka"
   :desc "Source namespaces load and run identically as an uberjar on the JVM and under babashka."
   :doc "### Scenario

The tool is started as a Leiningen uberjar or with the babashka launcher (bb.edn), and the tests run with bb test.

### Measure

The same sources work under both runtimes, so no dependency may be unavailable in babashka (e.g. no clj-http) and JVM-only classes need a workaround (the JsonProcessingException Class/forName fix). Source: dev/plans/deps-dev-vulnerability-adapter.md.

### Quality attribute

Portability."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/configurable-policies
   :name "configurable policies"
   :desc "License and vulnerability policies are set in a policy file, not in code."
   :doc "### Scenario

A team changes which licenses are whitelisted, greylisted or blacklisted, or which vulnerability severities block a build, by editing a policy file.

### Measure

No code change or rebuild is needed to change a policy. Source: AGENTS.md (\"Policies must be configurable\").

### Quality attribute

Flexibility."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/extensible-formats-and-sources
   :name "extensible formats and sources"
   :desc "SBOM formats, policy formats, report formats and vulnerability sources can be added without changing the core."
   :doc "### Scenario

A developer adds an SBOM format or version, a report format or a vulnerability source (e.g. NVD).

### Measure

The change consists of a new adapter namespace that registers with an existing multimethod; domain and application code stay unchanged. Source: AGENTS.md (\"Other formats/versions could be added\"), dev/plans/nvd-vulnerability-adapter.md.

### Quality attribute

Extensibility and modifiability."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/untrusted-input-as-data
   :name "untrusted input is handled as data"
   :desc "SBOM, VEX and policy files are parsed as data and never evaluated."
   :doc "### Scenario

The tool reads an SBOM, VEX or policy file from an untrusted source.

### Measure

Input is parsed with data readers only. Malformed input produces a typed error, not a crash or code execution. Source: dev/plans/vex-openvex-adapter.md (VEX files are as user-controlled as SBOM files), AGENTS.md (security starting points). This has not been reviewed in the code yet.

### Quality attribute

Security."
   :tags #{"quality"}}

