  ;; Proposed security requirements, derived from the security assessment at commit 5279795.
  ;; They state target behavior that the code does not meet yet (see the linked risks).
  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/safe-report-output
   :name "report output is safe to render"
   :desc "Untrusted text in reports is escaped for the output format, and only http(s) URLs become links."
   :doc "### Scenario

A report built from an untrusted SBOM or from external service data is rendered in a CI summary, wiki or PR comment.

### Measure

Component names, license names and advisory text cannot add markup, and link targets with schemes other than http and https are not rendered as links. Verifiable with a test SBOM that carries markdown and javascript: URLs. Not met yet (see risk unsanitized-markdown-output).

### Quality attribute

Security (output integrity)."
   :maturity :proposed
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/bounded-network-calls
   :name "network calls are bounded in time and size"
   :desc "Every live lookup request has a connect and request timeout and a response size cap, and a timeout counts as a failed lookup."
   :doc "### Scenario

A vulnerability service stalls, answers slowly or returns a huge body during a CI run.

### Measure

The run ends within a bounded time and memory use stays bounded. The timeout and size values are not defined yet and need a maintainer decision. Not met yet (see risk no-network-timeouts-or-size-limits).

### Quality attribute

Reliability and resource use, security (availability)."
   :maturity :proposed
   :tags #{"quality"}}

  {:el :requirement
   :id :sbom-tool.requirement/credentials-only-to-own-service
   :name "credentials are sent only to their own service"
   :desc "An API key is sent only to the host of the service it belongs to, over HTTPS, and is never printed or logged."
   :doc "### Scenario

A user supplies a GitHub or OSV API key through a key file or an environment variable.

### Measure

The key appears only in the Authorization (or X-Goog-Api-Key) header of requests to the service's own host. Followed URLs such as pagination links are checked against that host. The key is never written to stdout, stderr or reports. Partly met: not printed (inspected); host check missing (see risk pagination-url-not-pinned-to-host).

### Quality attribute

Security (confidentiality)."
   :maturity :proposed
   :tags #{"quality"}}

